// Deliberately does NOT `link "lzma"` — real bug found live by jensyleo
// (2026-08-05): that directive makes the linker embed a hard, unconditional
// `LC_LOAD_DYLIB` on liblzma (confirmed via `otool -L`: an absolute path,
// `/opt/homebrew/opt/xz/lib/liblzma.5.dylib`, baked into the binary) for
// EVERY consumer of ROMForgeCore, including the app itself — regardless of
// whether any CHD/LZMA code path is ever actually invoked. On any Mac
// without that exact file (no Homebrew, a different prefix, or `xz`
// uninstalled), the app fails to LAUNCH at all with a cryptic dyld error,
// never reaching any of ROMForge's own code. `CHDLZMADecompressor` now
// resolves the one real function it needs (`lzma_raw_buffer_decode`) via
// `dlopen`/`dlsym` at runtime instead (see `HomebrewDylibLoader`) — this
// header is still needed at BUILD time (for the `lzma_options_lzma`/
// `lzma_filter`/`lzma_ret` C type declarations ClangImporter bridges, which
// cost nothing at link time on their own), just no longer at *run* time.
module CLZMA [system] {
    header "shim.h"
    export *
}
